<title>UK: BA rise on hopes for U.S. aviation talks.</title>
<headline>BA rise on hopes for U.S. aviation talks.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British Airways Plc rose on Thursday ahead of free market aviation talks in the U.S. that could pave the way to its proposed link-up with American Airlines, traders said.</p>
<p>British Airways shares were up 18-1/2p at 636.5p by 1114 GMT. Volume in the stock reached 2.5 million shares.</p>
<p>Talks were due to resume in Washington later today between U.S. and UK aviation negotiators. Dealers said a shortage of stock in the market had exaggerated today's gains.</p>
<p>&quot;Hopes for an &quot;open skies' pact seem to have been pushing the stock a little and there has been a bit of a bear squeeze,&quot; said one market-maker.</p>
<p>-- Simon Gardner, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
